00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.989
Leah: We have touched on this already,
but all organisations that work with

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.130
children and young people should have
procedures and policies of safeguarding

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:13.519
in place to ensure that every child,
regardless of age, disability, gender

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.420
reassignment, race, religion or
belief, sex or sexual orientation

00:00:18.459 --> 00:00:20.280
has an equal protection from harm.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.119
Rhiannon: They should also be safe
from other children or adults who may

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.160
present a risk, wherever they are.

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.599
Abuse can potentially occur anywhere,
from voluntary, community or faith

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:36.309
groups, schools, hospitals and
sports clubs and even in the home.

00:00:37.109 --> 00:00:40.139
Leah: Specific safeguarding issues,
with children and young people

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:45.160
include, bullying, self-harm,
criminal exploitation, sexual

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.719
exploitation, grooming, domestic
abuse, drug exploitation and county

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:56.160
lines activities, radicalisation,
up skirting and sexting, forced

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.170
marriage, FGM and honour based abuse.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.340
Rhiannon: As many as 1 in 3 children
sexually abused by an adult, never

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:17.380
tell anyone, so it's crucial that even
those who only occasionally work with

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.740
children, should be aware of safeguarding
and child protection and what to do.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.610
Leah: If a person suspects that any
safeguarding issues have arisen, they

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.480
should record any information they can
and tell someone who can report it.

00:01:31.039 --> 00:01:34.419
This could be a friend, a
teacher, a family member, a social

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:38.450
worker, a doctor or healthcare
professional, a police officer or

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.130
someone else who can be trusted.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.560
Rhiannon: All children and young
people should be listened to and

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.220
not dismissed, but their rights also
need to be respected and situations

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.179
need to be handled sensitively and
appropriately by the proper authorities.

